  "summary": "This experiment tested an RNA-only multiprofile model with avgpool aggregation, achieving validation accuracy of 0.5907 and F1 of 0.5727, lower than the multimodal multiprofile baseline (config_004) of 0.6186 accuracy. The results suggest that multiprofile benefits may not be modality-agnostic, as RNA-only configurations underperform compared to multimodal counterparts. The relative impact of aggregation methods and profile settings remains uncertain without direct comparison to alternative strategies."
}

